course: dictionary
lesson: 5655
title: Who is a listener?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A listener is a person who listens to someone or something. You can be a listener in a classroom, at home, or in front of a radio. «Jesus explained the four soils as kinds of listener; only the good soil gave a big harvest.» Here the listeners are the people who hear the story and take it in.
explain: Listening well is more than just hearing. A good listener looks at the speaker, does not interrupt, and asks questions. «A clever listener hears both what happened and how the speaker feels about it.» So a good listener notices feelings as well as facts.
explain: Listener can also mean a person who listens to a radio programme or podcast. Radio stations talk to their «listeners», just as TV talks to «viewers». When you meet the word, look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means.
fact: A listener is a person who listens to someone or something.
fact: A good listener looks at the speaker, does not interrupt, and asks questions.
fact: «A parable» is a short story Jesus told about everyday life, with a deeper meaning about God and how to live.
fact: Listener can mean someone who listens to a radio programme or a podcast.
fact: Radio stations call their audience «listeners», just as TV calls its audience «viewers».
exercise: In a speaking and listening lesson, what is «a good listener»? | Someone who only hears the noise in the room | Someone who talks the whole time and never stops | Someone who is always looking at a phone | *Someone who looks at the speaker, does not interrupt and asks questions
exercise: «Radio stations talk to their listeners.» What is a listener in this sentence? | A person who plays the radio very loudly | A worker at a radio station who sells radios | *A person who hears a radio programme or podcast | A person who never switches the radio on
exercise: «A clever listener hears both what happened and how the speaker feels about it.» What extra thing does a clever listener notice? | The colour of the speaker's shoes | How many words the speaker uses | The date when the story happened | *How the speaker feels
test: Which word means a person who listens to someone or something? | viewer | speaker | *listener | soil
test: «A parable is a short story Jesus told about everyday life.» What is a parable? | *A short story with a deeper meaning | A kind of soil | A song about the weather | A long letter sent to a friend
exam: What clue in «Radio stations talk to their listeners» tells you listeners means the people who hear the radio? | like | their | talk | *Radio stations
